{"id": "EUVD-2026-81893", "enisaUuid": "99dbea60-141a-3f77-b405-3942504d3c0b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Clear buf on error in __bpf_get_task_stack\n\nBoth bpf_get_task_stack and bpf_get_task_stack_sleepable helpers that\nuse __bpf_get_task_stack have buf defined as ARG_PTR_TO_UNINIT_MEM\nargument and we should initialize the buf on every return path.\n\nAdding missing buf memset for __bpf_get_task_stack fail paths. This\nprovides deterministic buffer contents, which is useful when the buffer\nis used directly as a map key.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4acc761b4e3feca1eb648d21fc4d665b23c5372d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f5a7bcc049709af12e403111d5e73e80910dafc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f0f61573ba4cb899105b5cef65be3ca02205f93", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f523359c4789bb0396d2d642464a6e2fd4f2299d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5d242825ca417bb6afe35fde6e8880f97ca43fb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90300", "GHSA-ghq7-v2f8-82jr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b91e9c8-8d19-32cf-a001-0323b02c5c43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "06ab134ce8ecfa5a69e850f88f81c8a4c3fa91df <6f5a7bcc049709af12e403111d5e73e80910dafc"}, {"id": "1b5face5-db07-379c-ae2a-4d6d3881bab1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "06ab134ce8ecfa5a69e850f88f81c8a4c3fa91df <f523359c4789bb0396d2d642464a6e2fd4f2299d"}, {"id": "1d0b3e8f-6806-3cff-9516-f9d71e7719c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "06ab134ce8ecfa5a69e850f88f81c8a4c3fa91df <1f0f61573ba4cb899105b5cef65be3ca02205f93"}, {"id": "1ea0c2d2-ca9e-3b1b-8bd8-633ed3d614b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2aba7dc4-aae0-